/* Generated by Cozytile ({{label}}). GTK4 only; imported from gtk-4.0/gtk.css.
   GTK 4.24+ binds ext-background-effect on every toplevel but sends an empty blur region unless the
   window has a CSS backdrop-filter, and Hyprland then drops its own blur for that window. The filter
   makes GTK send the whole window as the blur region, so the compositor blur applies like it does for
   kitty or GTK3 apps. The radius is not used for the visible blur (Hyprland's settings are); values
   under about 8px make GTK skip the region. Empty while Frosted glass is off. */
{{#if frost}}window { backdrop-filter: blur(20px); }
{{/if}}
